          <SubComponents>
            <Component class="javax.swing.JTextArea" name="jTextArea1">
              <Properties>
                <Property name="background" type="java.awt.Color" editor="org.netbeans.beaninfo.editors.ColorEditor">
                  <Color blue="cc" green="cc" red="cc" type="rgb"/>
                </Property>
                <Property name="columns" type="int" value="20"/>
                <Property name="font" type="java.awt.Font" editor="org.netbeans.beaninfo.editors.FontEditor">
                  <Font name="Segoe UI" size="10" style="1"/>
                </Property>
                <Property name="rows" type="int" value="5"/>
                <Property name="text" type="java.lang.String" value="(Cool Facts About Sharks)&#xa;&#xa;1) Sharks have existed for over 400 million years&#xa; &#x2014; older than dinosaurs and even trees.&#xa;&#xa;2) They can detect a drop of blood in the water from &#xa;hundreds of meters away thanks to an extremely&#xa; advanced sense of smell.&#xa;&#xa;3) Some sharks, like the Greenland shark, can live for&#xa; over 250 years, making them one of the longest-living&#xa; vertebrates on Earth.&#xa;&#xa;4)Sharks don&#x2019;t have bones &#x2014; their skeletons are made&#xa; entirely of cartilage, which makes them flexible &#xa; and fast.&#xa;&#xa;5)The Whale shark, the largest fish in the world,&#xa; can grow longer than a bus and survive by eating &#xa;tiny plankton.&#xa;&#xa;(How Sharks Are Affected by Sea Pollution)&#xa;&#xa;Sharks are suffering heavily from the state of our &#xa;oceans. Plastic pollution breaks down into microplastics&#xa;, which settle into the bodies of smaller fish and &#xa;eventually into sharks when they eat them. &#xa;These toxins build up in shark tissues, weakening their&#xa; immune systems, harming reproduction, and making &#xa;them more vulnerable to disease. Abandoned fishing &#xa;nets (&#x201c;ghost nets&#x201d;) also trap and drown sharks, &#xa;especially species like reef sharks and tiger sharks.&#xa; Chemical runoff, oil spills, and declining fish&#xa; populations from overfishing all combine to make life &#xa;in the ocean more dangerous for sharks than ever &#xa;before."/>
              </Properties>
            </Component>
          </SubComponents>
        </Container>
      </SubComponents>
    </Container>
